      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Under aerobic conditions, pdmH2 (0.03 g, 0.2 mmol) and NEt3 (0.056 mL, 0.4 mmol) were dissolved in MeCN/MeOH (20 mL, 3:1 v/v). Solids Gd(NO3)3·6H2O (0.09 g, 0.2 mmol) and [Cu2(O2CCH2But)4(HO2CCH2But)2] (0.08 g, 0.1 mmol) were added together to the stirred pale-yellow solution. The blue suspension was stirred 30 min, filtered, and the filtrate was allowed to evaporate slowly at room temperature. After 20 days, X-ray-quality blue crystals of 1·3.4MeCN·0.4MeOH·0.7H2O were collected, washed with cold MeCN (2 × 3 mL) and Et2O (2 × 3 mL), and dried under vacuum (40% yield as solvent-free 1).",
